ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Qi Gong for 60+","url":"https://www.meetup.com/chi-of-thee-meetup-group/events/316651541/","description":"### Inviting Adults 60+ to Start Your Healing Journey with Pureland Qi Gong — On the Danforth\n\n**with Generational Qi Gong Master Teresa Yeung**\nAfter a lifetime of caring for your family, friends, and others, **it's time to care for yourself.**\nAt 69, Master Teresa Yeung understands that staying active and taking care of our body, mind, and spirit becomes increasingly important as we grow older.\nThis is your time to **nurture yourself, keep moving, and thrive in the years ahead.**\nThrough the gentle practice of **Pureland Qi Gong**, you will learn simple movements, breathing, and relaxation practices designed to support your body's natural balance, circulation, flexibility, and vitality.\n\n### Keep Your Body Moving. Keep Your Spirit Thriving.\n\nQi Gong offers a gentle way to continue being active while giving yourself time to slow down, breathe, and reconnect.\nYou will explore practices that can help you:\n\n* **Keep the body gently moving**\n* Support flexibility, balance, and coordination\n* Encourage relaxation and mindful breathing\n* Cultivate and circulate Qi (energy)\n* Develop greater awareness of your body\n* Create a regular practice for your own well-being\n\n**And you can practice both standing and seated.** You don't have to be on your feet for the entire class.\n\n### Your Next Chapter Can Be About You\n\nYou have spent much of your life taking care of others.\nNow, take one hour for **yourself**.\nJoin Teresa Yeung and other adults 60+ for a welcoming introduction to **Pureland Qi Gong** and discover a gentle practice you can continue to enjoy as you move forward in life.\n**You are never too old to start something new.**\n\n## A Special Introductory Class\n\nThis 1-hour class is an opportunity to **experience Qi Gong with Teresa before deciding whether you would like to continue**.\nIf there is sufficient interest, a **4-week Qi Gong program for adults 60+** may be offered following these introductory sessions.\nThere is **no obligation to register for the 4-week program**. Come simply to experience the class and see if Qi Gong is right for you.\n\n## 📍 In-Person Class — Toronto\n\n**Room 212 Danforth Avenue**\n**2nd floor of Carrot Common**\n**Toronto, Ontario M4K 1P1**\n\n### 📍 **Choose your Class**\n\n**Wednesday, October 14, 2026**\n🕥 **10:30 AM – 11:30 AM**\n**OR**\n**Thursday, October 22, 2026**\n🕑 **2:00 PM – 3:00 PM**\n\nPlease register for the date and time that works best for you. **Each class is a separate event.**\n\n### 💰 **Introductory Class Fee**\n\n**$20 + 13% HST = $22.60 total**\nThe introductory class fee is **$22.60 per person, including HST**.\n\n## What to Bring\n\n* Comfortable clothing\n* Water\n* A willingness to relax, breathe and enjoy the experience\n\nPlease arrive **10–15 minutes early** so you have time to settle in before the class begins.\n\n## Meet Your Teacher — Teresa Yeung\n\n**Generational Qi Gong Master Teresa Yeung** is the founder of Pureland International Qi Gong in Canada and a successor in the lineage of Grandmaster Weizhao Wu.\nWith more than **30 years of experience teaching Qi Gong internationally**, Teresa has shared Qi Gong with people from many different backgrounds and age groups.\nShe is the creator of **Wu's Eye Qi Gong®, Heart Chi Gong™ and the Hidden Pearl Series for Women**, and is a **3-time #1 internationally bestselling author**.\n\nAt 69, Teresa is especially interested in sharing Qi Gong with people in her own generation — helping them discover simple ways to keep moving, breathing and cultivating greater balance in everyday life.\nPurelandQiGong.com\n\n#carrotcommon\n#torontoqigongtaichi\n#seniors","startDate":"2026-10-22T06:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Pureland International Qi Gong","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Room 212, 348 Danforth Avenue (2nd floor Carrrot Common Plaza), Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Chi of Thee Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/chi-of-thee-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Chi of Thee Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Compost and Connect Social Hour","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-compost-circle-social-gathering-group/events/316525067/","description":"We are hosting a casual get-together for anyone in the city who is interested in composting, gardening, or just finding more ways to live sustainably. This is a low-pressure space to swap tips on managing a bin in a small apartment, share experiences with local community gardens, or simply meet others who care about reducing waste. Whether you are a total beginner who is curious about where to start or a seasoned composter with a heap in your backyard, you will find a welcoming crowd here.\n\nWe will be meeting up to chat, share stories, and maybe even trade some compost wisdom or leftover kitchen scrap solutions. There is no formal agenda or presentation; just bring yourself and an interest in making our city a little greener. If you have been looking for a way to connect with like-minded neighbors in Toronto, please pull up a chair and join us.\n\nIf you think you can make it, please let us know by sending an RSVP so we can get an idea of how many folks to expect. We look forward to seeing you there.","startDate":"2026-10-22T16:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"MP29+6J Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"MP29+6J Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Compost Circle Social Gathering Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-compost-circle-social-gathering-group/"},"performer":"The Compost Circle Social Gathering Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Coronation Street Meet Up","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-coronation-street-lovers/events/316707161/","description":"Do you watch Coronation street but have no one to talk to about the comings and goings of this classic UK show? Then come and have a natter over a pint or a cuppa with a group of CS fans!\n\nA positive, laid back group with the emphasis on fun. If you do not enjoy currently watching the show, this is not the meet up for you. No haters or grumps!!! 😃 Although we can all agree that we are glad someone finally bumped off Theo! 🤣\n\nThere might even be trivia…and perhaps prizes. All suggestions for time of day and venue preferences welcome. Please read group description to see if this is the group for you.","startDate":"2026-10-22T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Elephant & Castle","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"212 King St W, Toronto, ON M5H 1K5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Coronation Street Lovers!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-coronation-street-lovers/"},"performer":"Toronto Coronation Street Lovers!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free event. CBC Because News . Quiz show taping","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316555061/","description":"I took the group to a few of these already. Great times always.\n\n[Because News](https://www.cbc.ca/radio/becausenews/about-because-news-1.4344480) is Canada's funniest news quiz. Host and award-winning comedian Gavin Crawford makes games out of the headlines, along with a panel of comedians and celebrities.\n\nIt's also become [somewhat of a TikTok hit](https://www.niemanlab.org/2023/10/wait-wait-dont-tell-me-how-this-canadian-radio-show-became-a-tiktok-hit/)\n\nNote - very limited, sold out event. **Only sign up if you can 100% commit to attend.**\n\nMeet 6PM\nDoors open 6:30PM\nTaping should end around 8:30PM.\n\n**THIS GROUP IS OPEN TO THOSE THAT WANT TO BE SOCIAL, MAKE FRIENDS, THAT ARE SINGLE OR NOT SINGLE. WE ALSO HAVE LOTS OF OTHER EVENTS LIKE, MOVIES, WALKS, HIKES, ARTS & CULTURE AND RESTAURANTS. WE LOVE TO SUPPORT MEMBERS TO SOCIALIZE AND TO FORM LONG LASTING FRIENDSHIPS.**\n\n**Rules:** [Click Here!](https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/293241263/)\n**Getting The Best Out Of MeetUp:** [Click Here!](https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/293241269/)\n\nConsider [joining our Whatsapp](https://chat.whatsapp.com/JpUbpvfPcNuFzTJ1VqTLZO) to discuss this and future events too\n\nDon't Forget to join our email list (Meetup does not send out emails to\neveryone in a group) to get our weekly news later about upcoming events: [http://eepurl.com/hKt76f](http://eepurl.com/hKt76f)\nFacebook group @ [http://www.facebook.com/groups/502945113062739/](http://www.facebook.com/groups/502945113062739/)","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CBC News Network","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"250 Front St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Board Game Night!!!!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/events/316231712/","description":"Hello Meeples!!!!\n\nI host board game night every Thursday at Face to Face Games, located at 1398 Danforth Ave (about a 3 min walk from Greenwood station, or a 7 min walk from Coxwell station)! How it works I’ll be seated at the table at the very back right hand corner of Face to Face Games (near the washrooms).\n\nWe usually have 2 tables reserved for our group. (If you can’t find us, ask one of the staff members.) I’ll bring a variety of games from my own collection to board game night, but attendees are free to bring any of their own games as well! Got a brand new game you’ve been dying to play but never have enough players? Bring it along!\n\nGot a retro game that you think is a hidden gem? Bring it along and spread the joy! I usually come early at around 4:30pm. If there are other attendees who also arrive early, then we can play some shorter games until 6pm. Six o’clock is when the event officially starts and is when most attendees start trickling in.\n\nOnce we have most people assembled, we collectively decide which games we want to play and split into groups accordingly. We usually have one group tackling a heavy board game (ie. a game that tends to be more complex and takes longer to finish) while the others play short to medium-length games, but this is very flexible and will depend on turnout and the kinds of games people bring.\n\nIf you can only get here later or if you arrive late, don’t fret. We’ll see what game you can join so that you can get playing as soon as possible!\n\nRules of the Tables:\n\nWe are a cool and relaxed group - we swear! But to ensure things run smoothly and that everyone is having fun, we do some some rules we would like attendees to follow:\n\n\\- Please be respectful of people’s games and property\\. For example\\, if you’re having a snack \\(please share\\!\\)\\, make sure your fingers are clean before you handle cards\\, mats\\, meeples\\, and the like\\. People are generous to bring their games to board game night\\, so we want to be mindful not to damage or dirty their stuff\\.\n\n\\- Please be mindful of your cellphone usage during the game\\. Of course this doesn’t mean you can’t use your cellphone to shoot a quick text message or to check something quickly\\. we’re not monsters\\!\n\n\\- However\\, if you’re always focused on your cellphone \\(for example\\, watching a video or playing a cellphone game\\) and are not paying attention to the rules being explained\\, or you constantly need the other players to repeat themselves as to what sick moves they just made\\, then it ends up taking away from everyone’s enjoyment of the game\\.\n\n\\- Please be decent\\, in dress and in conduct\\. No bullying\\, excessive swearing\\, racist or sexist language\\, and all the other bad stuff\\.","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Geekz United","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/"},"performer":"Geekz United"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cafe Français au Black Pony - $3","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/events/316769304/","description":"(English below) Venez profiter de la bonne nourriture et d'une bonne conversation en français au café **Black Pony** situé au **1481 Gerrard St East.** Nous serons à l'arrière du café autour d'une grande table, prêts à vous accueillir.\n\nOn va pratiquer la langue de Molière tout en nous faisant de nouveaux amis(es)s. **Toutes les 30 minutes, nous changerons de place** pour favoriser les échanges. Tout le monde est bienvenu, quel que soit son niveau.\n\nPour en savoir plus sur le café et son menu délicieux et varié : [https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/](https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/)\n\nSi vous ne souhaitez pas que votre photo soit publiée sur MeetUp, veuillez en informer Vishnu.\n\n**Pourquoi ces frais de 3$?** C'est pour payer le coût de l'hébergement sur la plate-forme Meetup pour l’année courante et les années précédentes. Nous vous demandons de payer $3.00 à chaque événement. Vishnu sera là pour recueillir vos contributions. Nous vous prions de bien vouloir apporter de la monnaie.\n\nSi vous préférez, vous pouvez utiliser ce lien pour payer sur Square: [CLIQUER ICI](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nMerci,\n**Vishnu**\n\n..................................................................................................................\n\nCome and enjoy good food and good conversation at the **Black Pony café** located at **1481 Gerrard St East.** We'll be in the back of the café around a big table, ready to welcome you.\n\nWe'll be practicing the French language and making friends, **keeping in mind that every 45 minutes we'll be moving around to mix up the conversation.** Everyone is welcome, whatever your level.\n\nTo find out more about the cafe and its delicious and varied menu: https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/\n\nWhy the $3 fee? It helps cover the cost of hosting the group on the Meetup platform for the current year and previous years. We ask participants to contribute **$3.00 at each event**. Vishnu will be there to collect contributions, so please bring change.\n\nIf you prefer, you can use this Square link:\n[CLICK HERE](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nThank you,\nVishnu","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Black Pony Café and Snack Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1481 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Professionals & Investors Mixer: AI, Capital & Cash Flow","url":"https://www.meetup.com/phenom-society/events/316683716/","description":"Phenom Society hosts curated Toronto gatherings where business owners, operators, investors, and professionals exchange practical ideas and build valuable relationships.\n\n**Not a pitch night.** Not a guru seminar. Not a room full of people handing out business cards and hoping something happens.\n\n**The goal is simple:** bring useful people together around business, investing, financing, private markets, AI, and building in this economy.\n\nIf you’re growing a business, managing clients, looking at investment opportunities, trying to understand where AI fits into your work, or just want to meet serious people in Toronto, come through.\nWe’ll keep it casual, but intentional.\n\n**Expect:**\n\\- business owners\\, professionals\\, and investors\n\\- conversations around capital\\, AI\\, sales\\, financing\\, and investing\n\\- real networking without the weird pressure\n\\- people who are actually building\\, investing\\, or actively looking for better rooms\n\n**This is a good fit if you are:**\n\\- a business owner or founder\n\\- a professional interested in investing\\, business\\, or private markets\n\\- an investor or private\\-market curious professional\n\\- in sales\\, finance\\, real estate\\, lending\\, or professional services\n\\- building with AI or trying to understand how it applies to your work\n\\- looking to meet serious people in Toronto without the usual networking\\-event nonsense\n\n**This is probably not for you** **if** you’re looking for a get-rich-quick pitch, a crypto hype room, or a room where everyone is trying to sell each other immediately.\n\nThis event is for education, networking, and general discussion only.\nNothing shared should be taken as investment, legal, tax, or financial advice.\n\n**What happens:**\n6:30 PM — Arrival + casual networking\n7:00 PM — Short welcome / room framing\n7:10 PM — Open networking + real conversations\n8:30 PM — Wrap\n\n**Space is limited to 20 people** so the room stays small enough for real conversations.\n\n**RSVP** if you want to meet sharper people in Toronto building around business, capital, AI, and wealth.","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Toronto, ON, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Phenom Society | Business, Investing & Wealth Network","url":"https://www.meetup.com/phenom-society/"},"performer":"Phenom Society | Business, Investing & Wealth Network"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"French at the Royal Conservatory","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/316159559/","description":"Join us for an evening of French conversation at B Espresso Bar in the atrium of the Toronto Royal Conservatory of Music (near St. George station)! We welcome all levels of French, and it's free\\*. Venez pratiquer votre français!\n\n\\*While there is no fee to attend this event, guests are expected to purchase something from B Espresso Bar, in accordance with RCM's restrictions on usage of the cafe atrium space.\n\n**Building location:**\nThe Royal Conservatory is at 273 Bloor St W, between Varsity Stadium and the Royal Ontario Museum (ROM). There are entrances off Bloor St. and Philosopher's Walk. If you enter from Bloor St through the large glass doors, follow the hallway on the left beside the staircase and turn left at the end. (Closest TTC: St. George)\n\n**Notes and restrictions:**\nThe host may or may not attend this event. Attendees are encouraged to seat themselves at two or more adjacent tables, as needed. Please form groups of 6 people at each table; do not rearrange chairs and tables to accommodate more people, as this obstructs the narrow walking space. Guests are expected to order something from the cafe, and are asked to please refrain from bringing outside food or drink. Attendees must leave the building at 8pm when the cafe stops serving.\n\n**Contributions:**\nIf you are a regular with us and would like to support the group, please send any contributions by e-transfer to [diskutomeetup@gmail.com.](http://diskutomeetup@gmail.com.) The yearly donation goal and amounts received year-to-date will be tracked anonymously on [this google sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18GfqYsis8Cf2XGg4KsKQJsY_0Fv3bsSQHwJAxvC1Km8/edit?usp=sharing). Thank you so much for your support.","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Royal Conservatory of Music","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"273 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316200973/","description":"# 👻 Ghost Tour: The Exhibition Grounds 🎡\n\n### Toronto's Haunted Fairgrounds, Dark History & One Building I Don't Like Being Near\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds have spent more than a century hosting crowds, celebrations, soldiers, shows, and some of Toronto's biggest events.\nBut underneath all that history is a darker side.\n\nThe Exhibition Grounds are said to be **one of the most haunted places in Toronto** — and I'll be honest: **this is the one place on my ghost walks that genuinely scares me.**\n\nThere's something about the atmosphere here.\nSome buildings have an energy that feels different. And when you know what happened in them, it's hard not to look at them a little differently.\n\nOn this evening ghost walk, we'll explore the grounds and hear stories of **soldiers, settlers, performers, animals, tragedies, and people who may never have completely left.**\n\nThis isn't just about trying to scare you.\nIt's about discovering the strange history hiding underneath one of Toronto's most familiar landmarks.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside **Medieval Times** and make our way across the Exhibition Grounds toward the Princes' Gates.\nAlong the way, we'll hear stories connected to:\n\n* 🏚️ **The General Service Building**\n* 💀 **The Stanley Barracks** — the building that genuinely creeps me out\n* 🐎 **The Horse Palace**\n* 🏠 **Scadding Cabin**\n* 👻 Other strange stories, unexplained encounters, and haunted corners of the grounds\n\nWe'll finish at the **Princes' Gates**.\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace and **will not be entering any of the buildings**.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ Why This One Is Different\n\nI've done a lot of ghost walks around Toronto.\n**This is the one that actually makes me uncomfortable.**\nMaybe it's the history. Maybe it's the buildings. Maybe it's simply knowing what happened here and then standing there after dark.\n\nWhatever it is, the Exhibition Grounds have always felt different to me.\n\nSo come prepared for some genuinely creepy stories — and maybe a few moments where we all wonder whether we should really be standing there. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** In front of **Medieval Times**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Princes' Gates**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**, rather than one of our regular social walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these walks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\nAnd maybe… don't wander off by yourself. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone fascinated by Toronto's darker history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🎡 People who want to see the Exhibition Grounds differently\n* 🚶 Anyone looking for something unusual to do on an evening out\n* 😈 People who like being scared — at least a little\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just have to be willing to walk into the dark with us.**\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**And try not to look too closely at the buildings.** 👻","startDate":"2026-10-22T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Medieval Times Dinner & Tournament","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"10 dufferin Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"📕October’s book: The Surrogate Mother","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-women-s-book-society/events/316176952/","description":"Join us for a cozy, spooky evening discussing The Surrogate by Freida McFadden! 🕯️🍂🎃 Come ready to share your thoughts, theories, and favorite twists while enjoying good conversation, drinks, and a little Halloween magic. 📚✨\n\nPlease update your RSVP no later than 48 hours in advance of the event, to ensure all members who would like to attend, have a fair chance of getting a spot. As per the groups policy, late cancellations and no-shows will be removed from the group.","startDate":"2026-10-22T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"La Plume","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"453 Wellington street west, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto women’s book club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-women-s-book-society/"},"performer":"Toronto women’s book club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fifteenth Meetup: Security Without the State – Police, Courts & the Free Market","url":"https://www.meetup.com/liberty-labs-toronto/events/316654741/","description":"Join Liberty Labs Toronto for our fifteenth meetup on **Thursday, October 22, 2026, at 7:00 PM** near Yonge and Eglinton!\n*(Note: this is one week later than our usual mid-month date.)*\n\nThis month we’re asking a hard question with an open mind: if there were no monopoly on force, what would protection and justice actually look like?\nWe’ll discuss:\n\n* How private security, insurance, and competing protection agencies might work in practice\n* How courts and dispute resolution could function without a state monopoly (arbitration, reputation, restitution)\n* Historical and real-world examples of non-state order\n* Common objections: “who watches the watchers?”, the poor, violent crime, and “what if the biggest gang wins?”\n* The difference between anarchic chaos and a market for law and security\n\nCome ready to think out loud. You don’t have to already believe a free-market justice system would work — you just have to be willing to examine the idea honestly.\nWhat to expect:\n\n* Open, respectful discussion (bring questions, doubts, and examples)\n* Complimentary appetizers\n* Everyone who attends will receive a million-dollar Zimbabwe note as a fun take-home reminder of real value vs. fiat illusions\n* Connect with 10-20 liberty-minded Torontonians\n\nVenue: Pickle Barrel (2300 Yonge St, at Yonge & Eglinton), right above Eglinton Station. Easy parking in the Yonge Eglinton Centre garage or nearby Green P lots.\nRSVP on Meetup or Eventbrite to save your spot.\n\nLeave the official script at the door. Let’s talk about justice and security as voluntary services — together.","startDate":"2026-10-22T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Pickle Barrel","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2300 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4P 1E4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Liberty Labs Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/liberty-labs-toronto/"},"performer":"Liberty Labs Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AI & Tech Networking Event in Toronto by Ascent Valley","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/events/316209326/","description":"Join founders, investors and tech talent at this curated **startup networking event in Toronto.**\n\nMeet ambitious builders, exchange ideas and discover new opportunities in a dynamic community environment.\n\n**RSVP: [Use this link](https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ai-tech-networking-event-in-toronto-by-ascent-valley-tickets-1998516985101?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true)**\n**Please note that RSVP is managed via Eventbrite to control attendee lists — don’t ignore it to avoid issues with on-site payment.**\n\n**🚀 Meet investors, founders, AI experts, operators, and immigrant entrepreneurs building the next generation of global companies.**\n\n* Share your project and get feedback.\n* Connect with capital.\n* Expand your network.\n* This is where conversations turn into partnerships.\n* Use our participant mini app to keep every contact and insight from the event — nothing gets lost.\n\n👥 Who You’ll Meet\n• Startup Founders\n• Angel Investors & VC firms\n• AI Experts\n• Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia & the UK\n• Marketers, Sales leaders & Business Advisors\n• Builders & Game Changers\n\nStartup Pitch Session\nSelected founders take the stage for a focused 5-minute presentation in front of active investors and tech leaders.\nEach startup receives:\n⚡ Professional evaluation\n⚡ Investor feedback\n⚡ Visibility inside our global ecosystem\n\n**Why You Can’t Miss It**\n• Meet Tech & Business professionals, founders, and active investors\n• Gain real feedback from venture capitalists and angel investors\n• Discover new opportunities in AI, Tech & early-stage startups\n• Build meaningful connections in a global entrepreneurial community\nIf you’re serious about startups — you should be in the room.\n\n📈 Want to Pitch?\nSend your deck to:\n📧 events@ascentvalley.club or fill [form](https://ascentvalley.com/pitch)\nLimited spots. Curated selection.\n\n🏆 The startup recognized as “Most Investment-Worthy” will be featured across our social media and included in our investor newsletter.\n\n**🌟 About Ascent Valley**\n\n[Ascent Valley ](https://ascentvalley.com/infrastructure \"https://ascentvalley.com/infrastructure\")is a global ecosystem connecting founders, innovators, and investors.\nWe believe great ideas shouldn’t stay hidden — they deserve to be heard, challenged, and supported by the right people.\nOur mission is to create environments where ambitious builders connect, collaborate, and grow together.","startDate":"2026-10-22T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Blood Brothers Brewing","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"165 Geary Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/startup-networking-founder-ecosystem-toronto/"},"performer":"Startup Networking & Founder Ecosystem | Toronto"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/e/4/4/highres_536252324.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" as="image" imageSrcSet="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/fallbacks/redesign/event-cover-3.webp?w=640 1x, https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/fallbacks/redesign/event-cover-3.webp?w=828 2x" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/5/d/9/highres_536301977.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/d/4/1/highres_517027489.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/a/7/d/highres_502779549.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/0/2/f/highres_530044143.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/8/7/7/highres_536286263.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/0/a/c/highres_468028844.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/a/c/9/highres_535755049.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/6/6/e/highres_535894414.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/6/5/highres_528122661.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/7/9/a/highres_535762426.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><meta name="next_csrf" content="bb83dca0-43ac-486e-8312-64dd0aca2859"/><script>(